# Plan: Add global settings panel with Yolo mode toggle

## Overview

Implement a global header bar with settings popover containing Yolo mode toggle. The header consolidates action buttons (project picker, new task dropdown) from TaskList and adds a settings icon that opens a shadcn Popover. Yolo mode persists via electron-store and passes `--dangerously-skip-permissions` flag to Claude CLI when enabled.

This follows the existing Computer/Capability/Orchestrator architecture with Vue state in orchestrators only, using the createContext pattern for injection.

See full specification: tasks/001/spec.xml

## Technical Approach

**Why this approach:**
- Reuses existing settings module infrastructure (capability + orchestrator pattern at `apps/gui/src/settings/`)
- Adds yoloMode to existing StoreSchema rather than creating new storage
- Settings orchestrator already holds Vue refs - just extend it with `yoloMode: Ref<boolean>`
- PTY capability accepts yoloMode as parameter, passes flag to spawn args

**Key patterns being followed:**
- Settings persistence: electron-store pattern at `apps/gui/electron/main/index.ts:23-41`
- Orchestrator state: ref pattern at `apps/gui/src/settings/settings.orchestrator.ts:57-59`
- IPC bridge: preload exposes API at `apps/gui/electron/preload/index.ts:8-9`
- createContext provider: pattern at `apps/gui/src/lib/utils.ts:37-85`

**Breaking Changes:**
- TaskList header buttons removed (FolderOpen, New+ dropdown) - moved to AppHeader
- ptyRunCommand IPC signature changes to accept yoloMode boolean
- Terminal orchestrator needs settings orchestrator injected for yoloMode access

