## Testing Strategy

- **Automated:** TypeScript compilation validates all type changes are consistent across layers (env.d.ts, preload, capability, orchestrator)
- **Manual:**
  - Toggle Yolo mode on/off, verify popover interaction works
  - Close/reopen app, verify setting persisted
  - Run Claude command with Yolo on, verify flag in PTY console log
  - Run Claude command with Yolo off, verify no flag
  - Verify AppHeader buttons work (project picker, create task, discover)
- **Regression:**
  - Existing terminal functionality still works
  - Panel resizing still works
  - Task selection still works
  - Settings persistence for projectPath and panelSizes still works

## Edge Cases

- Yolo mode toggled while command running — no effect on current command, applies to next spawn
- Settings popover closed by clicking outside — standard Popover behavior, no special handling
- Multiple rapid toggles — each calls setYoloMode which persists, final state wins

## Potential Pitfalls

- **IPC signature mismatch** — env.d.ts and preload must have identical signatures; update both in same task (task 6)
- **PTY flag format** — Must be separate array element, not embedded in command string; `['--dangerously-skip-permissions', command]` not `['--dangerously-skip-permissions ' + command]`
- **DI ordering in App.vue** — terminal orchestrator needs settings passed in; create settings first, then terminal with settings injected
- **Ref vs value** — In terminal orchestrator, read `settings.yoloMode.value` not `settings.yoloMode`
